  "prompt": "Extraction after download does not work correctly (incomplete data)\n\n**Describe the bug**\nDownloaded products are sometimes incompletely extracted (e.g. HRSEVIRI folder contains only EOPMetadata.xml, the .nat file is missing).\nA batch of 30 HRSEVIRI products was downloaded with eodag, and every download was reported as successful. Processing then found only 6 usable .nat files.\nThe other 24 extracted product folders contained only EOPMetadata.xml. The .zip archives next to them were complete and did contain the .nat.\nRe-running the download did not fix it. eodag treats the products as already downloaded (record in <output_dir>/.downloaded/) and returns the incomplete folders straight away.\nA later clean download of 2 products reproduced it: one extracted folder held only the .nat and the other only EOPMetadata.xml.\n\n**Code To Reproduce**\n\n```py\nimport os\nos.environ['EODAG__DEDL__AUTH__CREDENTIALS__USERNAME'] = 'user'\nos.environ['EODAG__DEDL__AUTH__CREDENTIALS__PASSWORD'] = \"pw\"\nos.environ['EODAG__DEDL__DOWNLOAD__OUTPUT_DIR'] = 'msg'\nos.environ['EODAG__DEDL__DOWNLOAD__MAX_WORKERS'] = '4'\n\nfrom eodag import EODataAccessGateway, setup_logging\n\nsetup_logging(3)\ndag = EODataAccessGateway()\n\nsearch_results = dag.search(\n             collection=\"MSG_HRSEVIRI\",\n             datetime=\"2026-07-11T00:00:00Z/2026-07-11T01:00:00Z\",\n             provider=\"dedl\",\n             extract=True, \n             delete_archive=False\n         )\nprint(f\"Found {len(search_results)} products\")\n\nfor product in search_results:\n    dag.download(product)\n```\n\n**Environment:**\n - Python version: `3.12`\n - EODAG version: `4.9`",
